{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "chatcmpl-tool-b8f4bc63afbbbf70", "type": "tool_result", "content": "# SemanticVocoder: Bridging Audio Generation and Audio Understanding via Semantic Latents\narXiv: 2602.23333\nAuthors: Zeyu Xie, Chenxing Li, Qiao Jin, Xuenan Xu, Guanrou Yang, Wenfu Wang, Mengyue Wu, Dong Yu, Yuexian Zou\nYear: 2026 | Venue: \nTopic: vocoder\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. SemanticVocoder directly generates waveforms from semantic latents, eliminating reliance on VAE modules and their associated negative impacts.\n  2. The text-to-audio system powered by SemanticVocoder achieves state-of-the-art performance on AudioCaps with a Fréchet Distance of 12.823 and a Fréchet Audio Distance of 1.709.\n  3. SemanticVocoder bridges audio generation and understanding by enabling both tasks to be modeled within a shared semantic latent space.\n\nTags: Vocoder, Vocoder/Diffusion\n===\n# WavFlow: Audio Generation in Waveform Space\narXiv: 2605.18749\nAuthors: Feiyan Zhou, Luyuan Wang, Shoufa Chen, Zhe Wang, Zhiheng Liu, Yuren Cong, Xiaohui Zhang, Fanny Yang, Belinda Zeng\nYear: 2026 | Venue: \nTopic: \nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. WavFlow introduces a simplified architecture that synthesizes high-fidelity audio directly in raw waveform space using waveform patchify, x-prediction flow matching, and specialized signal preprocessing to eliminate the need for audio tokenizers.\n  2. An automated data curation pipeline is developed to harvest large-scale, high-quality video-text-audio triplets to address the sensitivity of direct waveform modeling to data quality and scale.\n  3. Empirical validation demonstrates competitive results on VGGSound and AudioCaps benchmarks, proving that end-to-end raw waveform generation matches or exceeds the performance of established latent-based methods.\n\nTags: TTS, TTS/架构-NAR-Flow", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "d38295fa-d1d9-438f-92d3-e425bdae9b8c", "uuid": "4796b49d-1279-41ea-a127-0e388d4ecce4", "timestamp": "2026-08-05T08:31:25.198Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "# SemanticVocoder: Bridging Audio Generation and Audio Understanding via Semantic Latents\narXiv: 2602.23333\nAuthors: Zeyu Xie, Chenxing Li, Qiao Jin, Xuenan Xu, Guanrou Yang, Wenfu Wang, Mengyue Wu, Dong Yu, Yuexian Zou\nYear: 2026 | Venue: \nTopic: vocoder\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. SemanticVocoder directly generates waveforms from semantic latents, eliminating reliance on VAE modules and their associated negative impacts.\n  2. The text-to-audio system powered by SemanticVocoder achieves state-of-the-art performance on AudioCaps with a Fréchet Distance of 12.823 and a Fréchet Audio Distance of 1.709.\n  3. SemanticVocoder bridges audio generation and understanding by enabling both tasks to be modeled within a shared semantic latent space.\n\nTags: Vocoder, Vocoder/Diffusion\n===\n# WavFlow: Audio Generation in Waveform Space\narXiv: 2605.18749\nAuthors: Feiyan Zhou, Luyuan Wang, Shoufa Chen, Zhe Wang, Zhiheng Liu, Yuren Cong, Xiaohui Zhang, Fanny Yang, Belinda Zeng\nYear: 2026 | Venue: \nTopic: \nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. WavFlow introduces a simplified architecture that synthesizes high-fidelity audio directly in raw waveform space using waveform patchify, x-prediction flow matching, and specialized signal preprocessing to eliminate the need for audio tokenizers.\n  2. An automated data curation pipeline is developed to harvest large-scale, high-quality video-text-audio triplets to address the sensitivity of direct waveform modeling to data quality and scale.\n  3. Empirical validation demonstrates competitive results on VGGSound and AudioCaps benchmarks, proving that end-to-end raw waveform generation matches or exceeds the performance of established latent-based methods.\n\nTags: TTS, TTS/架构-NAR-Flow", "stderr": "", "interrupted": false, "isImage": false, "noOutputExpected": false}}
